(ns kotoba.kir.definition-identity
  "Canonical identity for typed Kotoba definitions (CI1).

  This is deliberately not a source, package, or Wasm hash.  It identifies a
  closed checked definition's canonical typed KIR and direct definition
  identity closure.  Authority is still supplied exclusively by package policy
  and the capability runtime.

  ## Scope: every checked definition, effectful or not

  The scope is `:closed-deterministic-checked-definition`
  (`lang/code-identity.edn`, owner decision 2026-09-02).  An effectful
  definition is in scope: its effect row is one of the sealed inputs, so a
  definition requiring `#{:host/http}` has an identity, and it is a different
  identity from the same KIR with an empty row.  The frozen vectors
  `:effect-row-http` and `:effect-row-two` in `lang/code-identity-vectors.edn`
  have said so since payload version 2; only the prose said \"pure\".  A CID is
  still never authority — `lang/typed-eval.edn` requires a receipt to
  *evaluate* an effectful definition by CID, and that receipt is the
  capability runtime's, not this namespace's.

  ## Effect-row vocabulary: named operations as keywords (bridged 2026-09-02)

  `effect-row-problem` admits a set of keywords and nothing else.  The
  compiler's `infer-effects` (kotoba-sema `frontend.cljc`, `direct-facts` /
  `normalize-effect-ceiling`) produces rows whose members are the wire form
  `[:cap/call <id>]` — vectors, not keywords — so a row taken straight from
  the compiler is refused here with \"definition effect row members must be
  keywords\" and gets no CID.  That refusal is deliberate and stays: the
  sealed row carries the SEMANTIC vocabulary — the named operations
  (`:state/transact`, `:clock/now`, `:host/http`) — because the numeric id is
  wire ABI, not source vocabulary (`lang/code-identity.edn` `:ability
  :source-model`: \"numeric IDs and portable envelopes are elaboration
  targets\"; `lang/capability-catalog.edn`: `:numeric-id :not-user-facing`).
  A catalog renumbering must not move a definition's identity, and a
  definition's identity must not depend on which wire ABI a backend speaks.

  Control effects are the exception, and they are the exception because there
  is nothing to translate.  `:abort` (the typed abort ability, kotoba-lang
  `lang/abort-ability.edn`) has no capability and no wire id: the compiler
  emits the bare keyword, which is already the sealed vocabulary, so the
  bridge passes it through unchanged.  It must reach the sealed row — a
  function that can abort has interface `[:result T E]` where one that cannot
  has `T`, and two definitions that differ in that must not share an identity.
  The set of such keywords is closed (`control-effects`); any other keyword is
  still refused as not a wire capability call.

  The bridge is `effect-row-from-hir`: it takes what the compiler reports —
  `{:effects #{[:cap/call 8] :abort ...} :named-operations #{:state/transact ...}}` —
  and the catalog's `id->name` (kotoba-sema owns the catalog and depends on
  this repository, so the mapping is an argument, never a lookup made here),
  and returns the keyword row.  A wire id the catalog cannot name is refused
  with the exact message \"effect row wire id has no catalog name: [:cap/call
  N]\" — never guessed, never carried through as a vector.  The encoding of
  keyword rows is untouched: every frozen vector in
  `lang/code-identity-vectors.edn` hashes to the same bytes it did before the
  bridge, which the test suite asserts vector by vector.

  ## What the identity seals

  `lang/code-identity.edn` names the canonical input:

      [:typed-kir :profile-version :desugar-contract-version
       :effect-row :interface :direct-definition-dependencies]

  All six participate.  Two of them are the reason this namespace exists at
  version 2:

  - **`:definition/effect-row`** is the authority the definition requires.  A
    payload that omits it gives two definitions with *different* effect rows
    the same identity, so a lock pinning the pure one would admit the
    effectful one.  The effect row is part of the semantic contract, not
    metadata about it.
  - **`:definition/desugar-contract-version`** is sealed because the ADR
    requires that \"a definition CID must never claim semantic equivalence
    across profile, type-rule, or canonical-KIR-version changes\".  Desugaring
    is what produces the KIR being hashed; if its contract moves, identical
    KIR no longer means identical meaning.

  ## Why the bytes are real DAG-CBOR

  Version 1 hashed `(pr-str canonical-edn)` and labelled the CID `dag-cbor`.
  Both halves were wrong.  The block did not decode as dag-cbor, and `pr-str`
  is not byte-identical across Clojure and ClojureScript, so the same
  definition could hash differently per implementation — which CI1's admission
  rule (\"byte-for-byte deterministic identity\") and CI6's cross-implementation
  conformance both forbid.

  Version 2 normalizes to a closed, injective, tagged form and encodes it with
  a deterministic CBOR encoder.  Every value carries its type tag, so a
  keyword can never collide with the string of the same name.  Numbers are
  carried as exact decimal/hex *text* rather than CBOR integers because a
  64-bit KIR literal exceeds the JavaScript exact-integer range: text keeps
  `:clj` and `:cljs` on the same bytes.

  Identity payloads are versioned, and version 2 CIDs are deliberately not
  version 1 CIDs."
  {:kotoba/export [canonical-bytes canonical-hex definition-cid definition-message identity-payload normalize payload-version]}
  (:require [kotoba.form :as form]
            [cbor.core :as cbor]
            [multiformats.core :as mf])
  (:schemas {:form/r [:record :form/r [[:tag :i64] [:s :string] [:n :i64] [:k :keyword]
                                       [:kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:span :i64] [:data :bytes]]]}))



(defn payload-version [] :i64 2)

;; ns/name of a keyword, as the host `stable-name` prints it (`keyword-name`
;; answers the name part only).
(defn- stable-name [k :keyword] :string
     (let [text (document-edn-print (document-keyword k))]
       (string-substring text 1 (string-byte-length text))))

(defn- refuse-form [] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [refused (assert (= 1 0))] (form/nil-form)))

(defn- tagged1 [tag :string] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-vec (form/one-form (form/string-form tag))))

(defn- tagged2 [tag :string payload [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-vec (form/two-forms (form/string-form tag) payload)))

(defn- hex-digit-at [n :i64] :string
     (string-substring "0123456789abcdef" n (+ n 1)))

(defn- bytes-hex-from [data :bytes i :i64 out :string] :string
     (if (>= i (bytes-count data))
       out
       (let [v (bit-and (bytes-at data i) 255)]
         (bytes-hex-from data (+ i 1)
                         (string-concat (string-concat out (hex-digit-at (u64-shift-right v 4)))
                                        (hex-digit-at (bit-and v 15)))))))

(defn- hex-nibbles [bits :i64 k :i64 out :string] :string
     (if (< k 0)
       out
       (hex-nibbles bits (- k 1) (string-concat out (hex-digit-at (bit-and (u64-shift-right bits (* 4 k)) 15))))))

(defn- ascii-lower-from [s :string index :i64 out :string] :string
     (if (= index (string-byte-length s))
       out
       (let [c (string-code-point-at s index)
             width (if (< c 128) 1 (if (< c 2048) 2 (if (< c 65536) 3 4)))]
         (ascii-lower-from
          s (+ index width)
          (string-concat
           out
           (if (if (>= c 65) (<= c 90) false)
             (string-substring "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" (- c 65) (+ (- c 65) 1))
             (string-substring s index (+ index width))))))))

(defn- hex-char? [c :i64] :bool
     (or (and (>= c 48) (<= c 57))
         (or (and (>= c 65) (<= c 70))
             (and (>= c 97) (<= c 102)))))

(defn- all-match-hex? [s :string i :i64 n :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i n)
       true
       (if (hex-char? (string-code-point-at s i))
         (all-match-hex? s (+ i 1) n)
         false)))

(defn- all-digits? [s :string i :i64 n :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i n)
       true
       (let [c (string-code-point-at s i)]
         (if (and (>= c 48) (<= c 57))
           (all-digits? s (+ i 1) n)
           false))))

;; -?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)
(defn- integer-text? [s :string] :bool
     (let [n (string-byte-length s)
           start (if (and (> n 0) (= (string-code-point-at s 0) 45)) 1 0)]
       (if (>= start n)
         false
         (if (= (string-code-point-at s start) 48)
           (= n (+ start 1))
           (if (and (>= (string-code-point-at s start) 49) (<= (string-code-point-at s start) 57))
             (all-digits? s (+ start 1) n)
             false)))))

;; the wrapper of an f64 / i64 literal: a one-entry map whose key is the
;; wrapper keyword and whose value is text. Answers the text, or nil-form.
(defn- wrapper-text [value [:ref :form/r] wrapper :keyword] [:ref :form/r]
     (if (and (= 9 (form/tag-of value)) (= 2 (form/count-of value)))
       (let [k (form/nth-of value 0)
             v (form/nth-of value 1)]
         (if (and (= 4 (form/tag-of k)) (= 3 (form/tag-of v)))
           (if (= (form/keyword-value k) wrapper) v (form/nil-form))
           (form/nil-form)))
       (form/nil-form)))

(defn- f64-literal-text [value [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [v (wrapper-text value :kotoba.lang.code-identity/f64)]
       (if (= 3 (form/tag-of v))
         (let [s (form/string-value v)]
           (if (and (= 16 (string-byte-length s)) (all-match-hex? s 0 16)) v (form/nil-form)))
         (form/nil-form))))

(defn- i64-literal-text [value [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [v (wrapper-text value :kotoba.lang.code-identity/i64)]
       (if (= 3 (form/tag-of v))
         (if (integer-text? (form/string-value v)) v (form/nil-form))
         (form/nil-form))))

;; --- order over the normalized domain -------------------------------------

(defn- rank [f [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [t (form/tag-of f)]
       (if (= t 0) 0 (if (= t 1) 1 (if (= t 3) 2 (if (= t 7) 3 4))))))

(defn- sign [n :i64] :i64
     (if (< n 0) -1 (if (> n 0) 1 0)))

(defn- cmp-form [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [ra (rank a)
           rb (rank b)]
       (if (not (= ra rb))
         (if (< ra rb) -1 1)
         (if (= ra 1)
           (sign (- (form/int-value a) (form/int-value b)))
           (if (= ra 2)
             (sign (string-compare (form/string-value a) (form/string-value b)))
             (if (= ra 3)
               (cmp-kids a b 0)
               0))))))

(defn- cmp-kids [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] i :i64] :i64
     (let [na (form/count-of a)
           nb (form/count-of b)
           n (if (< na nb) na nb)]
       (if (= i n)
         (sign (- na nb))
         (let [c (cmp-form (form/nth-of a i) (form/nth-of b i))]
           (if (= c 0)
             (cmp-kids a b (+ i 1))
             c)))))

(defn- sort-key [x [:ref :form/r] by-first :i64] [:ref :form/r]
     (if (= by-first 1) (form/nth-of x 0) x))

(defn- insert-position [sorted [:list [:ref :form/r]] x [:ref :form/r] by-first :i64 i :i64] :i64
     (if (>= i (vector-count sorted))
       i
       (if (< (cmp-form (sort-key x by-first)
                        (sort-key (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] sorted i) by-first))
              0)
         i
         (insert-position sorted x by-first (+ i 1)))))

(defn- rebuild-with [sorted [:list [:ref :form/r]] x [:ref :form/r] p :i64 i :i64 acc [:list [:ref :form/r]]]
     [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count sorted)
           acc1 (if (= i p) (form/append-form acc x) acc)]
       (if (< i n)
         (rebuild-with sorted x p (+ i 1) (form/append-form acc1 (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] sorted i)))
         acc1)))

;; A stable insertion sort: an item goes after every item that is not greater.
(defn- sort-fold [items [:list [:ref :form/r]] by-first :i64 i :i64 sorted [:list [:ref :form/r]]]
     [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (if (>= i (vector-count items))
       sorted
       (let [x (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] items i)]
         (sort-fold items by-first (+ i 1)
                    (rebuild-with sorted x (insert-position sorted x by-first 0) 0 (form/no-forms))))))

;; --- normalization -----------------------------------------------------------

(defn- normalize-list [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64 acc [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (if (>= i (vector-count kids))
       acc
       (normalize-list kids (+ i 1)
                       (form/append-form acc (normalize (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids i))))))

(defn- normalize-pairs [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64 acc [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (if (>= (+ i 1) (vector-count kids))
       acc
       (normalize-pairs kids (+ i 2)
                        (form/append-form
                         acc
                         (form/form-vec
                          (form/two-forms (normalize (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids i))
                                          (normalize (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids (+ i 1)))))))))

(defn- normalize-map [value [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [f64-text (f64-literal-text value)]
       (if (= 3 (form/tag-of f64-text))
         (tagged2 "f64" (form/string-form (ascii-lower-from (form/string-value f64-text) 0 "")))
         (let [i64-text (i64-literal-text value)]
           (if (= 3 (form/tag-of i64-text))
             (tagged2 "int" i64-text)
             (tagged2 "map"
                      (form/form-vec
                       (sort-fold (normalize-pairs (form/kids-of value) 0 (form/no-forms)) 1 0 (form/no-forms)))))))))

(defn normalize
     "A Form -> the closed tagged Form. See the host `normalize`; what it throws
     on, this traps on."
     [value [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [tag (form/tag-of value)]
       (cond
         (= tag 0) (tagged1 "nil")
         (= tag 1) (tagged2 "bool" value)
         (= tag 2) (let [n (form/int-value value)]
                     (if (and (<= (- 0 9007199254740991) n) (<= n 9007199254740991))
                       (tagged2 "int" (form/string-form (string-from-i64 n)))
                       (refuse-form)))
         (= tag 3) (tagged2 "str" value)
         (= tag 4) (tagged2 "kw" (form/string-form (stable-name (form/keyword-value value))))
         (= tag 5) (tagged2 "sym" (form/string-form (form/symbol-value value)))
         (= tag 11) (tagged2 "bytes" (form/string-form (bytes-hex-from (form/bytes-of value) 0 "")))
         ;; an f64 leaf (bits in n) is the f64 literal of the host wrapper: 16 lowercase hex digits
         (= tag 10) (tagged2 "f64" (form/string-form (hex-nibbles (form/bits-of value) 15 "")))
         (= tag 9) (normalize-map value)
         (= tag 8) (tagged2 "set"
                            (form/form-vec
                             (sort-fold (normalize-list (form/kids-of value) 0 (form/no-forms)) 0 0 (form/no-forms))))
         (= tag 7) (tagged2 "vec" (form/form-vec (normalize-list (form/kids-of value) 0 (form/no-forms))))
         (= tag 6) (tagged2 "list" (form/form-vec (normalize-list (form/kids-of value) 0 (form/no-forms))))
         :else (refuse-form))))

;; --- definition shape ----------------------------------------------------------

(defn- key-of [name :string] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/keyword-form (keyword-from-string name)))

(defn- field [definition [:ref :form/r] name :string] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-get definition (key-of name)))

(defn- has-field? [definition [:ref :form/r] name :string] :bool
     (form/form-has? definition (key-of name)))

(defn- positive-int? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (= 2 (form/tag-of f)) (> (form/int-value f) 0)))

(defn- all-keywords? [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i (vector-count kids))
       true
       (if (= 4 (form/tag-of (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids i)))
         (all-keywords? kids (+ i 1))
         false)))

(defn- base32-alphabet-char? [c :i64] :bool
     (or (and (>= c 97) (<= c 122)) (and (>= c 50) (<= c 55))))

(defn- all-base32? [s :string i :i64 n :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i n)
       true
       (if (base32-alphabet-char? (string-code-point-at s i))
         (all-base32? s (+ i 1) n)
         false)))

(defn- cid-text? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (if (= 3 (form/tag-of f))
       (let [s (form/string-value f)
             n (string-byte-length s)]
         (if (and (> n 1) (= 98 (string-code-point-at s 0)))
           (if (all-base32? s 1 n)
             (= 1 (bit-and (vector-at (mf/cid->bytes s) 0) 255))
             false)
           false))
       false))

(defn- all-cids? [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i (vector-count kids))
       true
       (if (cid-text? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids i))
         (all-cids? kids (+ i 1))
         false)))

(defn- dependency-repeats? [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64 j :i64] :bool
     (if (>= j (vector-count kids))
       false
       (if (= 0 (cmp-form (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids i)
                          (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids j)))
         true
         (dependency-repeats? kids i (+ j 1)))))

(defn- distinct-strings? [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i (vector-count kids))
       true
       (if (dependency-repeats? kids i (+ i 1))
         false
         (distinct-strings? kids (+ i 1)))))

(defn- missing-field [definition [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (not (and (has-field? definition "definition/profile-version")
               (has-field? definition "definition/desugar-contract-version")
               (has-field? definition "definition/kir")
               (has-field? definition "definition/effect-row")
               (has-field? definition "definition/interface")
               (has-field? definition "definition/dependencies"))))

(defn definition-message
     "What the host `definition-error` reports for the definition Form, as its
     message; the empty string when the definition is well formed."
     [definition [:ref :form/r]] :string
     (if (not (= 9 (form/tag-of definition)))
       "definition map required"
       (if (missing-field definition)
         "definition missing required field"
         (if (not (positive-int? (field definition "definition/profile-version")))
           "definition profile version must be positive integer"
           (if (not (positive-int? (field definition "definition/desugar-contract-version")))
             "definition desugar contract version must be positive integer"
             (let [kir (field definition "definition/kir")
                   row (field definition "definition/effect-row")
                   deps (field definition "definition/dependencies")]
               (if (not (= 9 (form/tag-of kir)))
                 "definition typed KIR map required"
                 (if (not (form/form-has? kir (key-of "op")))
                   "definition typed KIR must be an IR node with :op, not an arbitrary map"
                   (if (not (= 8 (form/tag-of row)))
                     "definition effect row must be a set"
                     (if (not (all-keywords? (form/kids-of row) 0))
                       "definition effect row members must be keywords"
                       (if (not (= 9 (form/tag-of (field definition "definition/interface"))))
                         "definition interface map required"
                         (if (not (= 7 (form/tag-of deps)))
                           "definition dependencies vector required"
                           (if (not (all-cids? (form/kids-of deps) 0))
                             "definition dependency CID required"
                             (if (not (distinct-strings? (form/kids-of deps) 0))
                               "definition dependencies must be unique"
                               ""))))))))))))))

(defn- put [acc [:list [:ref :form/r]] k [:ref :form/r] v [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (form/append-form (form/append-form acc k) v))

(defn identity-payload
     "The payload Form addressed by `definition-cid` (host: the payload map)."
     [definition [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-map
      (put (put (put (put (put (put (put (form/no-forms)
                                         (form/keyword-form :kotoba.definition-identity/version)
                                         (form/int-form 2))
                                    (form/keyword-form :profile-version)
                                    (field definition "definition/profile-version"))
                               (form/keyword-form :desugar-contract-version)
                               (field definition "definition/desugar-contract-version"))
                          (form/keyword-form :typed-kir)
                          (field definition "definition/kir"))
                     (form/keyword-form :effect-row)
                     (field definition "definition/effect-row"))
                (form/keyword-form :interface)
                (field definition "definition/interface"))
           (form/keyword-form :dependencies)
           (form/form-vec (sort-fold (form/kids-of (field definition "definition/dependencies")) 0 0 (form/no-forms))))))

(defn- canonical-fragment [definition [:ref :form/r]] :vector-i64
     (let [checked (assert (= "" (definition-message definition)))]
       (cbor/encode-form (normalize (identity-payload definition)))))

(defn canonical-bytes
     "The canonical DAG-CBOR block for the definition Form (a trap when it is
     malformed; ask `definition-message` first)."
     [definition [:ref :form/r]] :bytes
     (bytes-from-vector-i64 (canonical-fragment definition)))

(defn canonical-hex
     "Lowercase hex of `canonical-bytes`."
     [definition [:ref :form/r]] :string
     (mf/hexify (canonical-fragment definition)))

(defn definition-cid
     "The CIDv1 dag-cbor identity of the definition Form."
     [definition [:ref :form/r]] :string
     (mf/cidv1-dag-cbor (canonical-fragment definition)))


;; ---- the host reading (the JVM and nbb behaviour is unchanged) ----


nil

nil

nil

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; canonical normalization — a closed, injective, tagged value domain
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

;; ASCII-only lower-casing (f64 bits hex is [0-9a-fA-F]). `str/lower` is the
;; host Locale-dependent mapping and has no Kotoba twin; on the Kotoba route
;; only A-Z is folded, which is exactly what the hex payload needs.
nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

;; These keys are part of payload-v2's admitted source representation. They
;; deliberately retain the namespace of the pre-extraction authority: changing
;; them to auto-resolved ::f64/::i64 under this namespace would reinterpret old
;; frozen definitions as ordinary maps and therefore move their DefCIDs.
nil
nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

nil

;; A total order over the normalized domain, so sets and map keys have one
;; canonical sequence on every implementation. Deliberately not `compare` over
;; the source values: Clojure cannot compare a keyword with a string, and
;; `pr-str` ordering differs by platform.
nil

nil

nil

